    "repo": "swesmith/sunpy__sunpy.f8edfd5c",
    "problem_statement": "Map plotting fails with KeyError: 'title' when plot_settings contains title\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen a Map has a 'title' key in its plot_settings, calling plot methods like `plot()`, `peek()`, or `_repr_html_()` raises a KeyError for 'title'. This affects basic map visualization functionality.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sunpy.map\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Create a simple map with plot_settings containing title\nheader = {'cunit1': 'arcsec', 'cunit2': 'arcsec', 'ctype1': 'HPLN-TAN', 'ctype2': 'HPLT-TAN'}\ntest_map = sunpy.map.Map(np.random.rand(20, 15), header)\n\n# Add title to plot_settings\ntest_map.plot_settings['title'] = 'My Custom Title'\n\n# This should work but raises KeyError: 'title'\ntest_map.peek()\n```\n\nThe error occurs when trying to plot any map that has a 'title' key in its plot_settings dictionary. The issue affects multiple plotting methods including `plot()`, `peek()`, `quicklook()`, and `_repr_html_()`.\n\n#### Expected behavior\nMaps with custom titles in plot_settings should plot normally using the custom title.\n\n#### Actual behavior\nKeyError: 'title' is raised when attempting to plot."
  }
